---

Generate tasks for feature {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS — READ BEFORE STARTING:
- Tasks must NOT contain implementation code. No Go, Python, TypeScript, SQL, or any language code blocks.
- Each task file: 50-100 lines maximum (not counting frontmatter). If you exceed this, you are over-specifying.
- Tasks tell agents WHAT to build and WHERE to find design details — not HOW to code it.
- REFERENCE design doc sections (e.g., "See technical-spec.md Section 4.3 for interface contract") instead of copying content.
- After creating each task file, register it: shark related-docs add "<title>" <task-file-path> --task=<task-key>
- Also register feature-level docs if not already registered: shark related-docs add "<title>" <doc-path> --feature={{.id}}
- READ docs/plan/RULES.md for documentation standards.

CHECK COMPLEXITY TIER: Read feature metadata via {{template "get_json" .}} | jq -r '.metadata.complexity_tier'.

LOAD: specification-writing workflow write-task.md.

READ AVAILABLE DOCS:
(1) Feature description and triage report at {{.file_path}}
(2) Feature PRD if exists (prd.md)
(3) Architecture docs if exist (02-08 series)
(4) Test plan if exists (09-test-plan.md)
(5) Parent epic context
(6) docs/plan/RULES.md for documentation standards

Run write-task.md Step 0 (documentation detection).

ADAPT TO TIER:
- SIMPLE (typically no PRD/arch/test docs -- create 1-3 focused tasks directly from triage report and feature description, include acceptance criteria in task spec, reference existing patterns from triage)
- STANDARD (PRD + focused arch + test plan available -- create tasks per normal write-task.md process, typically 3-8 tasks)
- COMPLEX (full doc suite -- create comprehensive task breakdown per write-task.md, typically 8+ tasks with detailed dependency graph)

PRODUCE: Tasks via shark task create. Each task: goal, success criteria, design doc references (NOT copied content), test case references if test plan exists, validation gates, agent assignment, dependencies. For SIMPLE tier, embed test cases directly in task spec.

EXIT GATE varies by tier:
- ALL TIERS: Zero code blocks in any task file. Each task under 100 lines. All task files registered via shark related-docs add.
- SIMPLE (feature requirements covered by 1-3 tasks, AC clear)
- STANDARD (PRD requirements map to tasks, test cases mapped)
- COMPLEX (full write-task.md checklist, contract validation task if applicable)

Verify: {{template "list" .}}.
